      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $b$ onto $a.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 14+2\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}⟨3,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{13},0,\\frac{2}{13}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
